        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "04039d53-e974-5619-be30-bf79b9c75b02",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Regency Road, Adelaide; Klemzig; Dudley Park; Adelaide\n- Infrastructure: Muller Road; North East Road; Adelaide-Gawler railway line; Arndale Shopping Centre\n- Biology: Garrha limbata\n- Topics: geographic location; suburb boundaries; species distribution\n\nFacts:\n- Regency Road in Adelaide is located about 6 km north of the city centre.\n- Regency Road spans from Arndale Shopping Centre in Kilkenny in the west to Broadview in the east.\n- Regency Road continues east as Muller Road and ends at North East Road in Klemzig.\n- Klemzig is a suburb of Adelaide in the City of Port Adelaide Enfield.\n- Dudley Park is bordered to the north by Regency Road, to the south by Simpson Avenue, to the east by the Adelaide-Gawler railway line, and to the west by a north-south line from the Harrison Road-Simpson Avenue intersection to Regency Road.\n- Garrha limbata has been recorded in Australia from Queensland, New South Wales, the Australian Capital Territory, Victoria, and South Australia.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
